<title>INDIA: Indian soybeans, soyoil slide, but soymeal steady.</title>
<headline>Indian soybeans, soyoil slide, but soymeal steady.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-06-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices fell a further 100-150 rupees per tonne in central Indian markets on Monday as good arrivals of 1,300 tonnes met limited demand.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices dropped on heavy selling from plants and refineries. Soyoil solvent was down by 200 rupees and refined soyoil fell 500 rupees per tonne in thin trade.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices remained steady in very limited trading. Soymeal yellow was $310-311 per tonne FAS (Free alongside ship) west coast Indian ports for export. Rapeseed extraction was $112-113 per tonne FAS west coast Indian ports for exports and was 3,950-3,975 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on rail) condition. The undertone was steady.</p>
